
§§ `Hand-written cases: exact words of a charge`

-- s 377BG(2), using a child for the production of child abuse material
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BG(2)` `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) via 1`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did use, or cause or procure the use of, or, having the care or custody of, consent to or allow the use of, one Lim Mei Ling, a person below 16 years of age, for the production of material which you knew or had reason to believe was child abuse material, to wit, by the act charged, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 377BG(2) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 377BH(2), producing child abuse material
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BH(2)` `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) via 1`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did intentionally produce child abuse material, namely Lim Mei Ling, knowing or having reason to believe that it was child abuse material, to wit, by the act charged, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 377BH(2) of the Penal Code 1871."

§§ `s 377C(3)(c) - identifying the sex of a person`

-- (ii) a person who has undergone a sex reassignment procedure is identified as being of the sex to which that person has been reassigned
-- inputs: reassigned; the sex reassigned to; an identity card stating a sex; the sex it states
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` TRUE `the female sex` FALSE `the male sex` EQUALS JUST (`identified as the reassigned sex` `the female sex`)
-- reassignment wins over the identity card, which may still state the earlier sex
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` TRUE `the female sex` TRUE `the male sex` EQUALS JUST (`identified as the reassigned sex` `the female sex`)
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` TRUE `the male sex` TRUE `the female sex` EQUALS JUST (`identified as the reassigned sex` `the male sex`)
-- (i) the sex stated in the identity card at the time is prima facie evidence of the sex of that person
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` FALSE `the female sex` TRUE `the male sex` EQUALS JUST (`identified from the identity card` `the male sex`)
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` FALSE `the male sex` TRUE `the female sex` EQUALS JUST (`identified from the identity card` `the female sex`)
-- neither: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` FALSE `the female sex` FALSE `the male sex` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(c) the sex of the person` FALSE `the male sex` FALSE `the female sex` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the identity card gives prima facie evidence only; the reassignment does not
#ASSERT (`identified from the identity card` `the male sex`)'s `prima facie evidence only`
#ASSERT NOT ((`identified as the reassigned sex` `the male sex`)'s `prima facie evidence only`)

§§ `s 377C(3)(f) - the Illustration of a private act`

-- "A is showering in an open-concept shower cubicle at the changing room of a swimming pool and cannot reasonably expect not to
-- be casually observed. However, A has a reasonable expectation that A will not be surreptitiously recorded by a video camera."
-- inputs: reasonable expectation of privacy (against what was done); in a state of undress; using a toilet, showering or bathing; doing a sexual act
-- against casual observation A has no such expectation: A is not doing a private act, though showering
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(f) the person is doing a private act` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- against surreptitious recording A has one: A is doing a private act
#ASSERT `s 377C(3)(f) the person is doing a private act` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 377BB(9) - the presumption`

-- "Where A has made a recording of B doing a private act, or of B's genital region, breasts or buttocks in circumstances where they
-- would not otherwise be visible, B is presumed until the contrary is proved not to have consented to A making it."
#ASSERT `s 377BB(9) the effect of the recording` TRUE EQUALS `presumed, until the contrary is proved, not to have consented to A making the recording`
-- otherwise the subsection says nothing (a presumption limited by its own wording: NOTHING-kind, not "B consented")
#ASSERT `s 377BB(9) the effect of the recording` FALSE EQUALS `not covered by section 377BB(9)`

§§ `s 377BE(5) - the Illustrations of an intimate image or recording`

-- inputs: of B's genital or anal region; of B's breasts (B female); of B doing a private act; altered or generated to appear to show any of those;
-- so altered or generated that no reasonable person would believe it depicts B
-- Illustration (a): A copies, crops and pastes an image of B's face onto the image of a body of a person engaging in a sexual act; the image has been altered
-- to appear to show that B actually engaged in a sexual act. This is an intimate image.
#ASSERT `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Illustration (b): A pastes an image of B's face on a cartoon depicting B performing a sexual act on C. No reasonable person would believe that B was
-- performing the sexual act depicted on C. This is not an intimate image.
#ASSERT `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the three kinds in (a), each alone, unaltered
#ASSERT `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the exclusion is of an image "so altered or generated": a genuine image of B's genital region is not excluded
#ASSERT `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the limbs: "means ... and includes" does not say that anything else is not one (NOTHING-kind)
#ASSERT `s 377BE(5) the image or recording is an intimate image or recording` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 377BK(3) - the Illustration of possession of electronic child abuse material`

-- "Y has an online storage account ... Y has control of what is stored in the account ... Y uploads and stores electronic child abuse material.
-- Y has in his possession child abuse material."  inputs: the material is electronic; the person controls access to it
#ASSERT `s 377BK(3)(a) the person has the electronic child abuse material in his possession` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no control of access (a hard copy, or a file only someone else controls): the text's "if" is read as closed (marginal reading a)
#ASSERT `s 377BK(3)(a) the person has the electronic child abuse material in his possession` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) "may include": viewing or displaying by an electronic medium counts; another way is not said to be excluded
#ASSERT `s 377BK(3)(b) the way is a way of gaining access to material` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377BK(3)(b) the way is a way of gaining access to material` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 377BM(2) - the Illustrations of the defence of a protected purpose`

-- inputs: the charge is under 377BB, 377BC, 377BD or 377BE(1); the purpose was prevention, detection, investigation or punishment of an offence;
-- the conduct of proceedings or evidence for them; safety or national security; no intent to cause injury; reasonable cause; the image not kept longer than necessary
-- Illustration (a): A, a caregiver, forcefully opens the toilet door to find B in a state of undress, concerned for B's safety: "A has committed no offence".
#ASSERT `s 377BM(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Illustration (b): A keeps the mobile phone with the upskirt photograph with the intention of reporting the offence to the police, and hands it over: detection or investigation.
#ASSERT `s 377BM(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the same act kept longer than reasonably necessary: paragraph (b) fails
#ASSERT `s 377BM(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a purpose in paragraph (a) but with intent to cause injury, or without reasonable cause
#ASSERT `s 377BM(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 377BM(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- none of the purposes
#ASSERT `s 377BM(2) the defence of a protected purpose is made out` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 377BN(3) and (4) - the Illustrations of the defences`

-- inputs of (3): the charge is under 377BH to 377BK; the act has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art;
-- the act did not pose an undue risk of harm to any person below 16 years of age
-- Illustration (a): a university researcher has child abuse material in his possession for studying the psychological effects of exposure to it: legitimate purpose.
#ASSERT `s 377BN(3) the defence of a legitimate purpose is made out` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Illustration (b): a photo-journalist in a war zone takes a photo of a child victim of torture and submits it with an article for publication: legitimate purpose.
#ASSERT `s 377BN(3) the defence of a legitimate purpose is made out` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an undue risk of harm to a person below 16 takes the defence away
#ASSERT `s 377BN(3) the defence of a legitimate purpose is made out` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no legitimate purpose
#ASSERT `s 377BN(3) the defence of a legitimate purpose is made out` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Explanation: an act has a legitimate purpose related to art which reasonable persons would regard as art
#ASSERT `s 377BN(3) Explanation the act has a legitimate purpose related to art` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 377BN(3) Explanation the act has a legitimate purpose related to art` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) Illustration: A is 15 years old and takes a photo of herself alone posing in the nude, stored in her phone: "A has not committed the offence".
-- inputs: the charge is under 377BH to 377BK; the accused is below 16; the material is an image of the accused alone
#ASSERT `below 16 years of age` 15
#ASSERT `s 377BN(4) the defence of the child's own image is made out` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- at 16 the accused is not below 16
#ASSERT NOT (`below 16 years of age` 16)
#ASSERT `s 377BN(4) the defence of the child's own image is made out` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a photo that is not of A alone
#ASSERT `s 377BN(4) the defence of the child's own image is made out` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 377BO - the Illustrations (FORK DEF-B7)`

-- Illustration (a): A, a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, films in a foreign country a video recording of child abuse material
-- involving a person below 16 (B). B is in that foreign country during the filming. A is guilty under section 377BG or 377BH read with 377BO(1).
-- @fixture `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by filming B in a sexual pose on a visit to Batam"
-- T the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore
-- T the accused does the act outside Singapore
-- T the act involves a person below 16 years of age
-- T B is outside Singapore
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) via 1`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad`
#ASSERT `is guilty under section 377BO(1)` `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad`)'s section EQUALS "377BH read with 377BO(1)"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad`)'s offence EQUALS "child abuse material offence outside or partially outside Singapore"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) citizen films abroad`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, did outside Singapore an act which would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 377BH of the Penal Code 1871, involving one Lim Mei Ling, to wit, by filming B in a sexual pose on a visit to Batam, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 377BH read with section 377BO(1) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- Illustration (b): A, who is in Singapore, uses remote video facilities to film a video recording of child abuse material involving a person below 16 (B).
-- B is in a foreign country during the filming. A is guilty under 377BG or 377BH read with 377BO(2).  A is not said to be a citizen or a permanent resident.
-- @fixture `Abroad (b) in Singapore filming B abroad` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by filming B by remote video from Singapore"
-- T the accused does the act in Singapore
-- T the act involves a person below 16 years of age
-- T B is outside Singapore
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) via 1`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (b) in Singapore filming B abroad`
#ASSERT `is guilty under section 377BO(2)` `Abroad (b) in Singapore filming B abroad`
#ASSERT NOT (`is guilty under section 377BO(1)` `Abroad (b) in Singapore filming B abroad`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (b) in Singapore filming B abroad`)'s section EQUALS "377BH read with 377BO(2)"
-- Illustration (c): A, who is in a foreign country and is not a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, uses remote video facilities to film child abuse
-- material involving a person below 16 (B). B is in Singapore during the filming. A is guilty under 377BG or 377BH read with 377BO(3).
-- @fixture `Abroad (c) foreigner abroad filming B in Singapore` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by filming B by remote video from abroad"
-- T the accused does the act outside Singapore
-- T the act involves a person below 16 years of age
-- T B is in Singapore
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) via 1`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (c) foreigner abroad filming B in Singapore`
#ASSERT `is guilty under section 377BO(3)` `Abroad (c) foreigner abroad filming B in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT (`is guilty under section 377BO(1)` `Abroad (c) foreigner abroad filming B in Singapore`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (c) foreigner abroad filming B in Singapore`)'s section EQUALS "377BH read with 377BO(3)"
-- Illustration (d): A, who is in Singapore, uses computer software to alter and reproduce child abuse material which was not filmed in Singapore, stored in a
-- computer server in a foreign country which A accesses through A's computer in Singapore. A is guilty under section 377BH read with 377BO(7).
-- @fixture `Abroad (d) altering material from Singapore` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- S victim = "child abuse material stored on a foreign server"
-- S the manner = "by altering and reproducing it from Singapore"
-- T the accused does the act in Singapore
-- T the accused does in Singapore an act which is a physical element of the offence
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) via 1`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (d) altering material from Singapore`
#ASSERT `is guilty under section 377BO(7)` `Abroad (d) altering material from Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT (`is guilty under section 377BO(2)` `Abroad (d) altering material from Singapore`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (d) altering material from Singapore`)'s section EQUALS "377BH read with 377BO(7)"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (d) altering material from Singapore`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did in Singapore an act which is a physical element of an offence under section 377BH of the Penal Code 1871, involving one child abuse material stored on a foreign server, to wit, by altering and reproducing it from Singapore, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 377BH read with section 377BO(7) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- 377BO(5): in an exploitative relationship, A in Singapore does an act involving B of or above 16 but below 18 who is outside Singapore (377BL(2) or (3))
-- @fixture `Abroad (5) exploitative, B abroad` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by the act charged"
-- T the accused does the act in Singapore
-- T the act involves a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age
-- T B is outside Singapore
-- T A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) via 1`
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (5) exploitative, B abroad`
#ASSERT `is guilty under section 377BO(5)` `Abroad (5) exploitative, B abroad`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (5) exploitative, B abroad`)'s section EQUALS "377BL(2) read with 377BO(5)"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (5) exploitative, B abroad`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
-- 377BO(6): the same, doing the act outside Singapore with B in Singapore (here over 377BL(3))
-- @fixture `Abroad (6) exploitative, B in Singapore` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by the act charged"
-- T the accused does the act outside Singapore
-- T the act involves a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age
-- T B is in Singapore
-- T A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(3) via 1`
-- @end
#ASSERT `offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (6) exploitative, B in Singapore`
#ASSERT `is guilty under section 377BO(6)` `Abroad (6) exploitative, B in Singapore`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (6) exploitative, B in Singapore`)'s section EQUALS "377BL(3) read with 377BO(6)"
-- 377BO(4): (5) and (6) apply only where A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B: without it, neither applies
-- @fixture `Abroad (5) without the exploitative relationship` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- T the accused does the act in Singapore
-- T the act involves a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age
-- T B is outside Singapore
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) via 1`
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (5) without the exploitative relationship`)
#ASSERT NOT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (5) without the exploitative relationship`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (5) without the exploitative relationship`)'s text EQUALS ""
#ASSERT NOT ((`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (5) without the exploitative relationship`)'s refusal EQUALS "")
-- the geography is met but the act would not be an offence under 377BG, 377BH or 377BL(2) or (3) if done in Singapore
-- @fixture `Abroad (a) territorial limb only` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- T the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore
-- T the accused does the act outside Singapore
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) territorial limb only`)
#ASSERT NOT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) territorial limb only`)'s `made out`
-- the act would be an offence if done in Singapore, but no limb of 377BO applies (a foreigner, acting abroad, B not in Singapore)
-- @fixture `Abroad nothing geographic` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- T the act involves a person below 16 years of age
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) via 1`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 377BO` `Abroad nothing geographic`)
-- where the facts make out both 377BG and 377BH, the charge is framed under the first the text names: 377BG
-- @fixture `Abroad (a) both 377BG and 377BH` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- S victim = "Lim Mei Ling"
-- S the manner = "by the act charged"
-- T the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore
-- T the accused does the act outside Singapore
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) via 1`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) via 1`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BO` `Abroad (a) both 377BG and 377BH`)'s section EQUALS "377BG read with 377BO(1)"
-- nothing established
-- @fixture `Abroad nothing established` OF `Child Abuse Material Abroad Facts`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BG = `Child Abuse Material Use 377BG(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BH = `Child Abuse Material Production 377BH(2) nothing established`
-- E the act as an offence under section 377BL = `Exploitative Abusive Material 377BL(2) nothing established`
-- @end
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 377BO` `Abroad nothing established`)
